  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q23-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "$g(x)=\\dfrac{2x+1}{x-1}$ and $h(x)=\\dfrac{x+3}{x-5}$\n\nFind an expression for $gh(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$gh(x)=\\dfrac{3x+1}{8}$, $x\\ne5$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}gh(x)&=\\frac{2\\cdot\\dfrac{x+3}{x-5}+1}{\\dfrac{x+3}{x-5}-1}\\\\&=\\frac{2(x+3)+(x-5)}{(x+3)-(x-5)}\\\\&=\\frac{3x+1}{8}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original function $h(x)$ requires $x\\ne5$. Also, $h(x)=1$ would require $x+3=x-5$, which has no solution, so there are no further exclusions.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 29
  },
